{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again","id":334417,"title":"Can a Spectre become a Wraith again?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-08T12:26:17-08:00","id":334417,"title":"Can a Spectre become a Wraith again?","content":"Sea of Shadows says no, they disappear, perhaps Transcend.<br /> <br /> Doomslayers say that if they haven't become completely Oblivion tainted, they might - so as I understand it, Shades, Nephwracks, Onceborns and perhaps Apparitions cannot do it.<br /> <br /> Is there another official rule?<br /> <br /> What do you think about a Spectre becoming a Wraith again? Has it happened in your game? How?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T12:34:00-08:00","id":334428,"title":"","content":"Dark Reflections: Spectres says maybe, so I guess thats the official answer. Once a spectre Psyche's permanent Composure reaches 10, the spectre achieves Redemption, and there is no official information on what that means. Redeemed spectres disappear instantly from the Labyrinth, but whether they reappear in the Shadowlands, Transcend or simply cease to exist is up to the individual ST and the needs of the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T14:59:47-08:00","id":334565,"title":"","content":"Orpheus does have the Orphan-Grinders, ghosts that became Spectres but eventually managed to overcome it and return to being a ghost, albeit not quite the same as they once were.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T15:02:32-08:00","id":334570,"title":"","content":"The Psyche serves the same role to a Spectre that the Shadow serves for a Wraith, and can eventually redeem them back to being a Wraith. And while it isn't WtO, Orpheus has &quot;Orphan Grinders,&quot; whose whole concept is &quot;former Spectres who had the willpower required to get better.&quot; In other words; possible, but very difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T16:00:41-08:00","id":334618,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. Of course you will generally only be able to make the journey to spectre-hood and back once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:21:12-08:00","id":334662,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the answer, people. In what book of the orpheus series are the orphan grinders described?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:23:54-08:00","id":334666,"title":"","content":"The Orphan-Grinders....<br /> <br /> as in, that's that the name of the book in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:56:33-08:00","id":334704,"title":"","content":"Indeed, the book is called <i>Orphan-Grinders</i>. Though keep in mind that Orpheus is a bit of a different beast from WtO, not everything meshes together. Another reason I'm interested to see Wr20's take on Orpheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T17:58:55-08:00","id":334707,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Orpheus was as much an evolution of Wraith as a successor to it, and it's helpful to bear in mind that Orpheus was only partially linked to the cWoD setting. It took place in it's own world, sort of, but had lots of homages, nods and hints to the cWoD.<br /> <br /> Which makes it even more interesting and exciting to see it take it's place in the cWoD proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T20:10:08-08:00","id":334775,"title":"","content":"Ok, kudos!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T08:38:53-08:00","id":336069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=334707#post334707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Orpheus was as much an <u><i><b>devolution</b></i></u> of Wraith</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected that for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T08:54:04-08:00","id":336073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=336069#post336069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corrected that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>I happen to think Orpheus was cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T10:12:55-08:00","id":336136,"title":"","content":"Can we not get into that? Both games have their positives and negatives. And while Orpheus may not be as deep as WtO, but it does have some truly excellent qualities to it and material that could work quite well with WtO and vice versa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T17:19:37-08:00","id":336495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=336069#post336069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corrected that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Devolution isn't a word. Evolution means change over time. It is neither a statement on possitive or negative qualities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T17:40:37-08:00","id":336512,"title":"","content":"You're mistaken, Lian. Devolution may be a term of no utility in contemporary biology, but it nevertheless means 'degeneration' (among other things).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1562-fikealox","name":"Fikealox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T18:47:57-08:00","id":336569,"title":"","content":"Once again, can we PLEASE not get into this argument. Both games have their flaws and merits. If you don't like Orpheus, that's fine, don't touch the material. But comments like that will only annoy and anger those people who are fans of Wraith and Orpheus and could lead to all-around unpleasantness. So can we please stop this before it gets out of hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T05:33:13-08:00","id":336956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=336069#post336069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Corrected that for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">That was unnecessary. Any further edition warring jabs like that will not be accepted. </span></b><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T08:42:27-08:00","id":337067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=336956#post336956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">That was unnecessary. Any further edition warring jabs like that will not be accepted. </span></b></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry my mistake didn't think that comparing two different games, as Orpheus has literally nothing in common with Wraith aside from involving ghosts, is considered edition warring. My point being it did not actually evolve anything from Wraith as it didn't really include anything from Wraith, including Shadows, Shadowlands, Tempest, Labyrinth etc. It removed all of the aforementioned without adding anything, except the Grandmaw or what ever it was called which was suddenly bigger than the Neverborn yet never even hinted at in Wraith or elsewhere in WoD before Orpheus which is kinda like in a murder mystery movie ending with the sudden revelation that the murderer was someone who had not even been seen, even in the background somewhere, during the whole movie.<br /> <br /> Besides it's claimed in Orpheus that this Grandmaws awakening also awakened the Neverborn with the latter being destroyed by the Grandmaw or something similar, this event would actually have devastated the Nephandi since most of their Masters would have just disappeared as they are merely the dreams of the Neverborn as you can see from Book of Madness Revised.<br /> <br /> This is the last I will speak of the matter though since it seems to be frowned upon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Spelling 12-11-2014, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T01:44:46-08:00","id":339852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=334428#post334428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dark Reflections: Spectres says maybe, so I guess thats the official answer. Once a spectre Psyche's permanent Composure reaches 10, the spectre achieves Redemption, and there is no official information on what that means. Redeemed spectres disappear instantly from the Labyrinth, but whether they reappear in the Shadowlands, Transcend or simply cease to exist is up to the individual ST and the needs of the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting for contemplation. The revelation of even one such redeemed spectre in the Shadowlands would be like the resurrection of someone in today's world. It may be possible that they depart the Labyrinth to a place between which is a Wyld version of the Shadowlands. Perhaps this could be the secret origin of the new souls among the ancient Fae - the redeemed from the Bringer of Harmony transcend to the recycling power of the Wyld at its darkest most nightmare generating glorious state. Granted this ties in better with CtL, but had to share the interesting idea. What if the souls of the Otherkin originated from Redeemed Spectres in whom the tie to humanity is tenuous at best if not broken? What if the True Fae were taking humans, creating Changelings, in order to redefine, find connection with, or otherwise comprehend the humanity to which they no longer relate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T06:39:08-08:00","id":339961,"title":"","content":"The concept of onceborn and neverborn is new to me. On another thread someone posted their notion that Tzimisce and Lasombra (&quot;primordial&quot; antediluvians) might be undergoing apotheosis into a onceborn. I&quot;ve seen the term online. Is there a stat block somewhere for a neverborn somewhere so I can see just what kind of nastiness an antediluvian might evolve into?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3814-g3taso","name":"g3taso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3814_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T07:31:39-08:00","id":339987,"title":"","content":"Nope, there's no stats for the Malfeans. They're basically death gods of Oblivion just as the Antediluvians, the true Antediluvians, are undead blood gods. They ungodly powerful and not something a typical group of PCs can handle so they've never been stat'ed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:34:51-08:00","id":340196,"title":"","content":"You could probably more easily stat an Antediluvian than a Malfean in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T15:06:02-08:00","id":340246,"title":"","content":"The Antedeluvians have nothing on the Malfeans. The Neverborn are terrible un-creatures that sprung into being as nothingness was turned into somethingness at the birth of creation. They long for a return to nonexistence, and loathe physical existence with an intense passion. Existence is pain to them, and they want nothing but the utter annihilation of everything and a return to the nothing that gave them birth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T19:07:31-08:00","id":370604,"title":"","content":"Oh a curious Question? Any idea how to justify a Spectre at Composure 8+ not just commiting suicide?<br /> <br /> as they are probaly miserable feeling the constant nagging of their psyche.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T20:40:10-08:00","id":370704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=370604#post370604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh a curious Question? Any idea how to justify a Spectre at Composure 8+ not just commiting suicide?<br /> <br /> as they are probaly miserable feeling the constant nagging of their psyche.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unresolved Dark Passions? Much like Wraiths who similarly hang on to their unlives despite their Shadows urging's thanks to their unresolved Passions. These are emotions strong enough to defeat death in the first place after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T03:29:53-08:00","id":370844,"title":"","content":"I may misremember, but somewhere (probably Dark Reflection or in the Pardoners Guild) is said clearly that there are Spectres that, through regaining enough Composure, shifted back to being wraiths (at least one is around in some Pardoners' warehouse)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T08:14:43-08:00","id":371049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/334417-can-a-spectre-become-a-wraith-again?p=334618#post334618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. Of course you will generally only be able to make the journey to spectre-hood and back once.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. While I didn't read enough Wraith to get a clear picture of it--and from the sound of things, there wasn't a clear picture of it to find there even if I had--Orpheus is explicit in noting that if an Orphan-Grinder falls back to spectre-hood, there's no coming back for them. They had one shot at redemption, blew it, and now they're a cenobite-esque thing that neither gets nor wants another chance.<br /> <br /> I don't remember the specifics, as all my Orpheus books are at home, but that's the gist of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T11:15:22-08:00","id":371264,"title":"","content":"In Doomslayers it is stated that one of the primary goals of the Martyr Knights is the redemption of Spectres, and that they have succeeded although as one of the Shadow Sidebars is quick to point out, their successes number in the single digits, they usually revert, and indeed it isn't quite clear whether it is actual redemption or just a prolonged state of Catharsis. Of course it is a shadow saying this so, grain of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}